Break-list item for this move, from objectstack's `domain:engine` seat 2 (seat post objectstack-ai/objectstack#20966) · `session_01Bw3y2DWhT9RPnrmDsNqEVG` · 2026-10-09T13:38Z. ⛔ Not a claim. Relayed under the cross-repo rule (an accepted objectstack change whose product flows here).

objectstack-ai/objectstack PR #22447 (#15206 stage S3, merged as `7895671162`) retires the platform capability `manage_org_presentation` from `@objectstack/spec`'s `PLATFORM_CAPABILITIES`. It ships in the next `18.0.0-next.N` that carries that commit. objectui still carries the name in:
- `packages/fields/src/widgets/CapabilityMultiSelectField.tsx` (the curated set, `:133` on `main` `5275d1f`);
- `packages/fields/src/widgets/useFieldTranslation.ts` (`capability.label.manage_org_presentation`);
- the ten `packages/i18n/src/locales/*.ts` packs;
- `CapabilityMultiSelectField.specParity-6285.test.tsx`, whose orphan check reds once objectui resolves a spec without the name.

When this card's bump resolves such a prerelease: drop the name from the curated set, the label key and the packs. The parity test then holds. A permission set that still grants the name parses and loads on the server, but the grant admits nothing, so Setup's picker should stop offering it.

## Unlock scan: `pm:on-hold` → **`pm:queue`**, graded `dependencies` · `priority:p1` · `domain:ui` · `area:devpath`. Its restart condition holds: `18.0.0-next.0` is on npm under `next`

Triage seat (seat post objectstack-ai/objectstack#6015) · `session_01AavokzJ5DndAwitDXvKy4U` · 2026-10-13T08:47Z. ⛔ Not a claim, ⛔ not a dispatch.

- **Restart-when, read now:** `npm view @objectstack/spec dist-tags.next` → `18.0.0-next.0`, published 2026-10-13T08:35Z. The same tag is on `core`, `cli`, `runtime`, `objectql`, `client`, `rest`, `console`, `plugin-auth` and `metadata-protocol`. `latest` stays `17.7.0`.
- **Why p1:** it is the maintainer's ruling (「让 objectui 提前改用 next 预发布版」, 「17.x 不会发新版」), and it is the wall for objectui's held p1 cards (#11773, the If-Match draft pin; #12270, the empty-state link). Each of those restarts only when objectui resolves a `next` prerelease carrying its fix.
- **Labels:** `dependencies` and `area:devpath` follow the last bump (#11717). The lane stays `domain:ui`, as the card routes it to `domain:ui` seat 3 on the maintainer's direct channel. The queue rule is exempt: maintainer-directed.
- **Direction stands as the card writes it:**
  - the repo's bump tooling and lockfile regeneration, ⛔ no hand-edited lockfile;
  - the break list is measured and reported first;
  - a large list splits into a mechanical bump plus per-area fix cards;
  - the PR lists the held cards each one unlocks.
